{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HEB",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our profession, Christ Jesus;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who was faithful to him that appointed him, as also Moses ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was faithful",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in all his house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was counted worthy of more glory than Moses, inasmuch as he who hath built the house, hath more honor than the house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For every house is built by some ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; but he that built all things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Moses verily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " faithful in all his house, as a servant, for a testimony of those things which were ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "afterwards",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to be spoken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Christ as a son over his own house: whose house are we, if we hold fast the confidence, and the rejoicing of the hope firm to the end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore (as the Holy Spirit saith, To-day if ye will hear his voice,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, in the day of temptation in the wilderness:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my works forty years.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I was grieved with that generation, and said, They do always err in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " heart; and they have not known my ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I swore in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take heed, brethren, lest there be in any of you an evil heart of unbelief, in departing from the living God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But exhort one another daily, while it is called To-day; lest any of you be hardened through the deceitfulness of sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are made partakers of Christ, if we hold the beginning of our confidence steadfast to the end;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "While it is said, To-day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts, as in the provocation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For some, when they had heard, did provoke: yet, not all that came out of Egypt by Moses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But with whom was he grieved forty years? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not with them that had sinned, whose carcasses fell in the wilderness?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And to whom did he swear that they should not enter into his rest, but to them that believed not?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HEB.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HEB.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So we see that they could not enter in because of unbelief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
